      "title": "Fix crash in capture_interface_stat_start.",
      "message": "Fix crash in capture_interface_stat_start.\n\nThe current code assumes that if deserialize_interface_list sets `err`\nto non-zero, then it also sets `err_msg`. This is not always the case,\ne.g.\n\n```\nGList *\ndeserialize_interface_list(char *data, int *err, char **err_str)\n{\n    /* ... */\n    if (data == NULL) {\n        ws_info(\"Passed NULL capture interface list\");\n        *err = CANT_GET_INTERFACE_LIST;  // sets *err, but not *err_str\n        return if_list;\n    }\n    /* ... */\n}\n```\n\nThis change works around the crash by initializing err_msg to NULL in\nthe calling code.\n\nFixes https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/issues/19586.\n",
      "author_name": "James Ring",
      "author_email": "sjr@jdns.org",
      "authored_date": "2024-01-09T21:31:44.000-08:00",
      "committer_name": "John Thacker",
